{"ref":"BDB, עֲמָלֵק","hw":"עֲמָלֵק","html":"<big><span dir=\"rtl\">עֲמָלֵק</span></big><sub>39</sub>  <strong>n.pr.gent. Amalek (</strong>on—ָ v. Lag<sup>BN 162</sup> Ba<sup>NB 160</sup><strong>)</strong>;—ancient people <a data-ref=\"Numbers 24:20\" href=\"/Numbers.24.20\">Nu 24:20</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, S. of Canaan—in Negeb <a data-ref=\"Numbers 13:29\" href=\"/Numbers.13.29\">13:29</a> (all JE), fierce and warlike Bedawin (cf. GASm<sup>Geogr. 282</sup> GFM <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:3\" href=\"/Judges.6.3\">Ju 6:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:33\" href=\"/Judges.6.33\">33</a>), foes of Isr. during Exodus <a data-ref=\"Exodus 17:8\" href=\"/Exodus.17.8\">Ex 17:8</a> + 6 times <a data-ref=\"Exodus 17\" href=\"/Exodus.17\">Ex 17</a> (E), <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:17\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.17\">Dt 25:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:19\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.19\">19</a>; later marauders in Isr. territory <a data-ref=\"Judges 3:13\" href=\"/Judges.3.13\">Ju 3:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:3\" href=\"/Judges.6.3\">6:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 6:33\" href=\"/Judges.6.33\">33</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 7:12\" href=\"/Judges.7.12\">7:12</a>; <a data-ref=\"Judges 10:12\" href=\"/Judges.10.12\">10:12</a>, defeated by Saul <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:48\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.48\">1 S 14:48</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 15:2\" href=\"/I_Samuel.15.2\">15:2</a> + times <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:28\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.28\">1 S 14:28</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 18\" href=\"/I_Samuel.18\">18</a>, and by David <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 30:18\" href=\"/I_Samuel.30.18\">30:18</a> (cf. <strong>adj.gent.</strong> infr.), <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 8:12\" href=\"/II_Samuel.8.12\">2 S 8:12</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 18:11\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.18.11\">1 Ch 18:11</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 83:8\" href=\"/Psalms.83.8\">ψ 83:8</a>; also <span dir=\"rtl\">הָע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 1:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.1.1\">2 S 1:1</a> (where read <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲמָלֵק</span> or <span dir=\"rtl\">הָעֲמָלֵקִי</span>, v. Comm.); <span dir=\"rtl\">ע׳</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 4:43\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.4.43\">1 Ch 4:43</a>; as grandson of Esau <a data-ref=\"Genesis 36:12\" href=\"/Genesis.36.12\">Gn 36:12</a> (P) = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 1:36\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.1.36\">1 Ch 1:36</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 36:16\" href=\"/Genesis.36.16\">Gn 36:16</a>; appar. connected with Ephr. territory <a data-ref=\"Judges 5:14\" href=\"/Judges.5.14\">Ju 5:14</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Judges 12:15\" href=\"/Judges.12.15\">12:15</a> infr.; yet GFM conj. <span dir=\"rtl\">עֵמֶק</span>).—On Amalek v. Nö<sup>Amalekites (1864)</sup>; <sup>Ency. Bi. s.v.</sup>.","next":"BDB, עֲמָלֵקִי","prev":"BDB, עָמֵל²"}